    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a public company headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, and trades under the ticker LUMN. It is also known as Lumen Technologies. The company describes itself as providing a global fiber network, secure networking, edge cloud, and AI-ready infrastructure to connect people, data, and apps. It calls itself the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy and says its fiber footprint reduces latency where it matters.\n\nThe company's website highlights several customer deployments. It says Arctic Glacier replaced manual operations with built-in automation. For the New York Yankees, it describes a programmable, consumption-based network with diverse 100G paths and automatic failover between Yankee Stadium and digital operations facilities in Tampa. It says American Family Care needed an AI-era network, and Lumen built a private, low-latency network designed for heavy AI workloads. The site also states that Prometheus Hyperscale anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady.\n\nLouisiana records show 57 legal matters involving the company. Its CIK is 0000018926.",
